id":"b18ecbd8-5e76-44f3-be84-f2dd183c0e61","position":{"commit_sha":"477eba96ca630cd8028dbd372c4bdb8d00b87ef6","position":"1786729154999020001-b18ecbd8-5e76-44f3-be84-f2dd183c0e61"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"26a48e77cd21a4ec773d62798b5e9e7745d4df64e11e81bfa312b0b1d5deff3d","event_uuid":"e012944e-d874-4023-a83b-0dd3e49e8068","position":{"commit_sha":"62455766b3a230c612db7da465c3ed3e38db0087","position":"1786729159950280001-e012944e-d874-4023-a83b-0dd3e49e8068"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implemented + landed for review as Gerrit change 1780. Design: _build_snapshot fans out over projects.json mapping keys (unseeded -> single configured project, byte-identical regression); active+done JQL pair AND all 3 enrichment passes run per project; per-query _ACLI_CEILING is inherently per-project. Enrichment split into _enrich_parents/_enrich_comments/_enrich_issuelinks (verbatim, complexity-gate clean) orchestrated by _enrich_project. Inbound creates stamped with bridge_project (jira-key prefix) + repos via new projects_store.resolve_inbound_bridge_fields. Held-out oracle test_fetch_multi_project.py (7 tests) GREEN + mutation-checked; full rebar_reconciler suite 2723 passed; mypy + ruff + module-size + complexity gates clean. Awaiting LLM-Review +1 / Verified +1.","timestamp":1786724776290676001}],"created_at":1786160096505602001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"aee2eae7-4470-4bd7-b2ff-32dd455203db","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"cef7-7ac5-18e6-41a3"},{"link_uuid":"a0de0e64-258b-4de7-9566-938a57cd019d","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"a33c-9001-9d86-4e59"},{"link_uuid":"13890e90-3c97-4005-83e4-288aaa7f68e2","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"dff5-77fa-e975-4488"},{"link_uuid":"8619233c-06f4-46c1-8c3d-0cafbea3566b","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"6660-fe79-217a-433e"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nThe inbound fetcher can only see one tracker project. `_build_snapshot` resolves a single\n`query_project` and builds one JQL pair — active and recent-done — from it\n(`fetcher.py:313-406`), then runs its three enrichment passes — parent, comment, issuelink maps\n— against that one project key (`fetcher.py:408-560`). A store that lists several projects in its\nmapping still ingests only one of them, and single-project enrichment would silently drop\nparent/comment/issuelink data for every project but one. Inbound-created tickets also never record\nwhich project they came from, so the `bridge_project`/`repos` fields added by cef7 stay unset on\ninbound tickets.\n\n## Approach\n\n**Fan out per project (fetcher.py).** Replace the single `query_project` with the store's project\nSET: `projects_store.read_projects(repo_root).keys()`. For EACH project, issue the existing\n`jqls_for(project)` pair AND run all three enrichment passes (`get_parent_map` / `get_comment_map`\n/ `get_issuelinks_map`) scoped to that project key, merging every result into the ONE shared\n`snapshot` dict (deduped by the existing `seen_keys`). This reuses `jqls_for` and\n`_validate_project_key` unchanged, so bug 626d's JQL-injection guard keeps applying to every key\nwith no new interpolation site, and the per-query truncation ceiling (`_ACLI_CEILING`, raising\n`SilentTruncationError`) stays scoped per project — a busy project cannot exhaust a shared budget\non behalf of the others. When the mapping is unseeded (empty), fall back to the single\n`[query_project]` list so the exact pre-change query pair and single enrichment pass are issued —\nsingle-project behaviour is byte-for-byte untouched.\n\n**Failure semantics across the fan-out.** Base-query exceptions (transport/network, malformed\nresponse, `SilentTruncationError`) propagate and fail the whole pass, exactly as today — fanning\nout multiplies failure points but each is fail-closed, so no partial snapshot is written. The\nthree enrichment passes keep their existing per-pass fail-open degradation (log + continue),\napplied independently per project; a `BackendPaginationStallError` still re-raises past the\nhandlers (a stalled pager is a truncated read).\n\n**Record source project + default repos (apply_inbound_records.py).** Provenance needs NO new\nchannel through the snapshot: the snapshot is keyed by jira key, `_apply_inbound_create` derives\n`jira_key = mutation.target`, and the CREATE writer `_inbound_create_write_create_event` ALREADY\nreceives `jira_key` and `repo_root`. The source project IS `jira_key`'s prefix (`DIG-123` → `DIG`,\nthe same `rsplit(\"-\", 1)[0]` idiom the fetcher's parent-key derivation uses). A new leaf helper\n`projects_store.resolve_inbound_bridge_fields(jira_key, repo_root) -> dict` returns\n`{\"bridge_project\": <prefix>, \"repos\": mapping.projects.get(prefix, {}).get(\"repos\", [])}`; the\ncreate site stamps both fields in ONE line — `create_data.update(...)` — beside the existing\n`creation_channel` stamp (`apply_inbound_records.py:221`). No signature change and no\n`apply_inbound.py` edit are required, and the net addition to `apply_inbound_records.py` (already\n797 LOC, near the 800 cap) is the import + the update call — two lines, staying under the cap.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/fetcher.py` — fan out the base JQL pair AND all three\n  enrichment passes once per configured project into the shared snapshot; per-project ceiling;\n  unseeded-mapping fallback to the single configured project.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/projects_store.py` — new `resolve_inbound_bridge_fields`\n  leaf helper (derive source project from the jira key, default repos from that project's mapping\n  entry).\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/apply_inbound_records.py` — stamp `bridge_project` + `repos`\n  at the CREATE write site via the helper (net +2 lines; module is near the size cap).\n- tests under `tests/`.\n\n## Testing\n\nTier per the shared standard's external-service row: a stateful verified fake fed\nproduction-shaped Jira fixtures. The fake must RECORD the queries and enrichment calls it issues,\nbecause \"one JQL pair AND one enrichment pass per project\" is itself the contract under test and is\ninvisible to a result-only assertion.\n\n- Happy path: a mapping with two projects issues exactly two JQL pairs and one enrichment pass per\n  project (parent/comment/issuelink), and the merged snapshot carries issues AND enrichment data\n  from BOTH projects.\n- Postcondition: each inbound-created ticket records its source project in `bridge_project` and its\n  `repos` equal that project's mapping entry; checked on tickets created from a two-project\n  fixture.\n- Ceiling is per project: one project exceeding `_ACLI_CEILING` raises `SilentTruncationError`\n  naming it, while a second under-limit project still ingests — proving the budget is not shared.\n- Empty result: a listed project returning zero issues contributes nothing and does not fail the\n  pass.\n- Single-project regression: an unseeded mapping issues the identical query pair and single\n  enrichment pass as before this change; checked by comparing recorded queries/calls.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] A two-project mapping issues one JQL pair AND one enrichment pass (parent/comment/issuelink\n      maps) per project in a single pass, with both projects' issues and enrichment data present in\n      the merged snapshot; checked by a fake transport recording issued queries and enrichment\n      calls and asserting the exact per-project counts and contents.\n- [x] Each inbound-created ticket records its source project in `bridge_project` and the repos from\n      that project's mapping entry in `repos`; checked by asserting both fields on tickets created\n      from a two-project fixture.\n- [x] The truncation ceiling applies per project, not as a shared budget; checked by a test where\n      one project exceeds it (raising `SilentTruncationError`) and a second under-limit project\n      still ingests successfully.\n- [x] A single-project (unseeded) mapping issues an identical query pair and single enrichment pass\n      to the pre-change behaviour; checked by a regression test comparing the recorded\n      queries/calls.\n- [x] A configured project returning zero issues does not fail the pass; checked by an\n      empty-result fixture.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/fetcher.py","reason":"fan out the base JQL pair and all three enrichment passes per configured project into the shared snapshot; per-project ceiling; unseeded fallback"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/projects_store.py","reason":"new resolve_inbound_bridge_fields helper: derive source project from jira key, default repos from that project mapping entry"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/apply_inbound_records.py","reason":"stamp bridge_project and repos at the inbound CREATE write site via the helper"},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_fetch_multi_project.py","reason":"per-project query pair and enrichment pass, per-project ceiling, source-project/repos stamping, single-project regression, empty-result"},{"path":".github/complexity-baseline.json","reason":"drain the now-stale _build_snapshot complexity ceiling left when the three enrichment passes were extracted into _enrich_parents/_enrich_comments/_enrich_issuelinks (repo test_complexity_baseline requires the committed baseline be fully drained)"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["depends_on","a33c-9001-9d86-4e59"],["depends_on","cef7-7ac5-18e6-41a3"],["parent","0e68-41eb-5782-4336"],["relates_to","6660-fe79-217a-433e"],["relates_to","dff5-77fa-e975-4488"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"0e68-41eb-5782-4336","parent_status_uuid":"b18ecbd8-5e76-44f3-be84-f2dd183c0e61","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"1734-7c6d-5a6a-48fd","ticket_type":"story","title":"Multi-project inbound fetch: per-project JQL fan-out and source-project recording","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["5ba5449b-ee14-4d07-bfb2-efe59e752a74","3aeb2130-5eb0-4c8b-9a2d-da2d6557ad09","55a9ae7a-8b73-415f-ae54-e1cacc7a8048","fca3d347-9931-4919-882f-3405a2947ef8","20fafdaa-df3f-4ca9-9e77-a99de958ea0d","883aba54-8b44-4c30-969a-87531ae34d23","13890e90-3c97-4005-83e4-288aaa7f68e2","feeb5c49-2c73-4be0-b310-c087fa6fcf08","bede00d2-4995-4281-b253-bfb2a5dc8287","8619233c-06f4-46c1-8c3d-0cafbea3566b","eb4e4793-fe37-4bf8-a8d1-fd7e4d612e36","b18ecbd8-5e76-44f3-be84-f2dd183c0e61","e012944e-d874-4023-a83b-0dd3e49e8068"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786731430844062454,"uuid":"99683c9e-6593-4f94-8c1f-a5a23d3f07bf"}